# Test: a plugin-process command's arguments are judged against the leaves the
# model declares before the engine asks the plugin, and only judged tokens reach
# it.
# VALIDATES: route R9 (Dispatcher.routeToProcess, internal/component/plugin/
# server/command.go) through the real entry point: `ze cli -c` over SSH to a
# daemon that forwards the command to an external SDK plugin process.
#   - `le test record-plugin` declares `show config cat`. The model declares a
#     mandatory id of 1..128 characters for it (internal/plugins/config-cli/
#     yang), and no builtin RPC serves it in the daemon (`ze show config cat`
#     runs in the client), so the plugin route is the only one that can judge
#     it. Every shipped plugin command that declares an argument
#     is also served by a builtin, which judges first (route R1), so none of
#     them can show this route refusing.
#   - The plugin answers "record-plugin received: " and the arguments it was
#     given, which no engine refusal contains, so the marker proves an accepted
#     value reached the process and its absence that a refused one did not.
# PREVENTS: a declared bound that constrains nothing on the plugin route. R9
# once forwarded every token unjudged, so a 129-character id, or no id at all,
# reached the plugin process.
#
# Method: the daemon runs one SSH server on 127.0.0.1 $PORT, which the CLI dials.

option=timeout:value=120s
option=env:var=ZE_CONFIG_DIR:value=.
option=env:var=XDG_DATA_HOME:value=.
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass

stdin=init-answers:terminator=EOF_INIT
admin
testpass
127.0.0.1
$PORT
EOF_INIT

tmpfs=plugin-route.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external record-plugin {
		run "le test record-plugin"
		encoder json
	}
}
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze init:stdin=init-answers:exit=0
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze start plugin-route.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.

# 129 characters: one past the bound, refused before the plugin is asked.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze cli -c "show config cat ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc"
expect=stderr:contains=length 129 out of range 1..128
reject=stdout:contains=record-plugin received

# No id: the mandatory leaf is missing, refused before the plugin is asked.
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze cli -c "show config cat"
expect=stderr:contains=required argument missing: id
reject=stdout:contains=record-plugin received

# 128 characters: at the bound, the id reaches the plugin.
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=ze cli -c "show config cat cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc"
expect=stdout:contains=record-plugin received: cccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
reject=stderr:contains=out of range

cmd=stop:seq=6:name=daemon:signal=term
